Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their possible use  
• `concept.concept_code`, `concept.vocabulary_id`, `concept.concept_id` : look‑up the drug concept that has RxNorm code **35208 (quinapril)**.  
• `concept_ancestor.ancestor_concept_id / descendant_concept_id` : grab every concept that is a descendant of quinapril (tablet strengths, combination packs, etc.).  
• `drug_era.drug_concept_id , drug_era.person_id` : find everyone ever exposed to any of those concepts.  
• `person.person_id` : universe of all simulated patients; needed for denominator in the percentage calculation.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
10 exploratory → incrementally‑complex SQLs
--------------------------------------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1. Description: Show the concept row whose RxNorm code is 35208 (quinapril)
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.concept`
WHERE vocabulary_id = 'RxNorm'
  AND concept_code = '35208'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: See how that concept is typed and whether it is already marked as standard
SELECT concept_id,
       concept_name,
       standard_concept,
       concept_class_id
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.concept`
WHERE vocabulary_id = 'RxNorm'
  AND concept_code = '35208';
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Pull *all* descendant concept_ids (includes itself) for quinapril
WITH quinapril AS (
  SELECT concept_id
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_synthetic_patient_data_omop.concept`
  WHERE vocabulary_id = 'RxNorm'
    AND concept_code = '35208'
